    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1418">

                <pb facs="0936" n="820" xml:id="pg820"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.52/311.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        Special Agent Carothers.</hi><anchor n="122"
                        xml:id="d1418-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-06-08">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 8, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Spanish Ambassador, this city, reports that Constitutionalists at Monterey are
                    levying discriminatory taxes against Spaniards and making unfounded arrests for
                    purpose of demanding ransom from Spaniards.</p>
                <p>Bring to attention of Carranza and urge that no discriminatory or confiscatory
                    action be taken against property of Spaniards and that they be not arrested
                    without good cause.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">W. J. Bryan</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1418-f1" n="122" type="source" xml:id="d1418-f1-content">
                <p>Similar telegram to the American Consul General at Monterey.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
